mGBA's ROM patch code (IPS, UPS, BPS) read its numbers as little-endian into native integers: on
a big-endian host (the PS3) every UPS and BPS checksum mismatched (no patch loaded) and IPS
offsets, sizes and its end marker were misread. Fields are now read in their file's byte order.
The IPS output size is also the input grown to the furthest record instead of always 16 MiB,
which cut 32 MiB ROMs short and padded small ones (ps3gba writes the result to a file).
Tested by tools/patch_test.sh on a little- and a big-endian CPU.

diff --git a/src/util/patch-ips.c b/src/util/patch-ips.c
